    {
      "id": "96e13da4-f87a-4af7-869d-991307ff2c8a",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -2816,
        96
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 608,
        "height": 704,
        "content": "# Connectively questions AI-based matching\nThis workflow allows you to fetch questions from Connectively and check if the questions match your background. If so, it sends a notification to your Telegram account with the question and AI-based reasoning.\n\n\n## How it works\n1. Runs every hour on a schedule.\n2. Logs in to [Connectively](https://www.connectively.us/experts/questions) via its API and fetches questions.\n3. Filters by Technology category and removes questions already seen in previous executions.\n4. Filters questions by asking an OpenAI-compatible model to decide whether to answer based on the background you provided.\n5. Sends the matched question to Telegram.\n\n## Setup\n- [ ] Fill the login & password for \"Authorize\" node. Hint: Credentials can be obtained from [here](https://www.connectively.us/api-integration/sign-up)\n- [ ] Fill your background at \"Message a model\" node\n- [ ] Fill your Telegram chat id at \"Send notification\"\n- [ ] Enjoy!\n\n## Customize\n- Since this workflow allows use any OpenAI-compatible model you can use even self-hosted LLMs through LM Studio like gemma-4-e4b\n- You can find more about Connectively API documentation [here](https://www.connectively.us/api-integration/documentation/free)"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
